{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "06U0", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-open}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0cca33d7a9ebb8d4a9420c3cb0470153e6d9fdd56941814633f798df8335ab52", "source_text": "Open morphisms", "source_text_hash": "sha256:43252e9b87b39a04cd511244589a48977040b451ad93c3f3b410e9af91959631", "unit_id": "tag:06U0:title"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06U0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-properties-section-properties-morphisms}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:dfaee67d46ddd4d888702445be4244f6d5bf5b01389aeba0ea95707e8ecf77c4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f31a3ad13bdcb0d6c1063ab6956d15ef4889f15e97823fe32c34a4a18a752621", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a morphism of algebraic stacks which is representable by\nalgebraic spaces. In\nProperties of Stacks, Section\n<REF_0001>\nwe have defined what it means for <MATH_0002> to be universally open.\nHere is another characterization.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:6b2bb585a25571adb3f22eb85a0ccaaec726d879df32d027e613cc4037712370", "unit_id": "tag:06U0:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "06U0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : \\mathcal{X} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{Z} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0004": "$|\\mathcal{Z} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}| \\to |\\mathcal{Z}|$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-properties-section-properties-morphisms}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\end{enumerate}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-characterize-representable-universally-open}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:9d5aeb9363e6c0460c4d8ca174db9b6e52fab48bca0eb728566dbe3f6bc86cf4", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:2865ad75445619604a64c90801fa3872b3b652ee4550c926a4b408bb6e236223", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of\nalgebraic stacks which is representable by algebraic spaces.\nThe following are equivalent\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> <MATH_0002> is universally open (as in Properties of Stacks,\nSection <REF_0001>), and\n<STRUCT_0003> for every morphism of algebraic stacks <MATH_0003>\nthe morphism of topological spaces\n<MATH_0004> is open.\n<STRUCT_0004>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:140607d66442899d4ab0032c07c8bd73c37f4d5f8be6ccc1f6988e6fd59da17d", "unit_id": "tag:06U1:statement"}
{"chapter": "stacks-morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "06U0", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{Z} \\to \\mathcal{Y}$", "MATH_0002": "$V$", "MATH_0003": "$V \\to \\mathcal{Z}$", "MATH_0004": "$V \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X} \\to V$", "MATH_0005": "$|V \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}| \\to |V|$", "MATH_0006": "$$\n\\xymatrix{\n|V \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}| \\ar[r] \\ar[d] &\n|\\mathcal{Z} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}| \\ar[d] \\\\\n|V| \\ar[r] & |\\mathcal{Z}|\n}\n$$", "MATH_0007": "$$\n|V \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}| \\longrightarrow\n|V| \\times_{|\\mathcal{Z}|} |\\mathcal{Z} \\times_\\mathcal{Y} \\mathcal{X}|\n$$", "MATH_0008": "$\\Rightarrow$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{stacks-properties-section-points}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:09aa1f8c8ad23cd19dc339d90766602caa1ad31ba2d799a54bf34d02f2619393", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:53299cc3a058fe1f28b9d3374283c73a954ce8fbbc5d2886ccf70c30ad96c3a8", "source_text": "Assume (1), and let <MATH_0001> be as in (2).\nChoose a scheme <MATH_0002> and a surjective smooth morphism <MATH_0003>.\nBy assumption the morphism <MATH_0004>\nof algebraic spaces is universally open, in particular the map\n<MATH_0005> is open. By\nProperties of Stacks, Section <REF_0001>\nin the commutative diagram\n<MATH_0006>\nthe horizontal arrows are open and surjective, and moreover\n<MATH_0007>\nis surjective. Hence as the left vertical arrow is open it follows that\nthe right vertical arrow is open. This proves (2).\nThe implication (2) <MATH_0008> (1) follows from the definitions.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c5aba490b2a55e77451a1195b678e5b2ab8100396d1d3090dd2c992b50b70150", "unit_id": "tag:06U1:proof"}
